{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And you shall say. Take heed.</b> Milra, from the pattern of שמרים (Isaiah 25:6), like ושקט הוא על שמריו (Jeremiah 48:11), and the meaning is: abide in your watch, for השמר in the sense of guarding is always mil'eil, and the proof is אל תירא:" "<b>And be quiet.</b> A verb in the pa'al [active] binyan, and the meaning is: your soul, or your people." "And these kings are likened to tails of smoking brands, like אוד מוצל מאש (Zechariah 3:2), and the meaning is that they are like what remains of a brand that gives off smoke but has no power to burn. Therefore, when their anger waxes hot, they are like tails — though בחרי אפם, yet בחרי אף they resemble tails:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The verse cited as ישעיהו כ\"ה ו' does not contain שמרים in the received text; the reference may be corrupt or point to a different verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:34.848662535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}